@startuml banking-context-map
title Moneykeeper — Banking Context Map

skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor<<core>> LightYellow
  BackgroundColor<<supporting>> White
  BackgroundColor<<generic>> WhiteSmoke
  BorderColor<<core>> GoldenRod
  BorderThickness<<core>> 2
}
skinparam shadowing false

rectangle "Monobank API" as Monobank <<generic>>
rectangle "Banking" as Banking <<supporting>>
rectangle "Ledger\n(Core)" as Ledger <<core>>
rectangle "Reference Data" as ReferenceData <<supporting>>
rectangle "Classification" as Classification <<supporting>>
rectangle "Integration Runtime" as Integration <<generic>>
rectangle "Reporting" as Reporting <<supporting>>

Monobank "U" -[#crimson,dashed]-> "D (ACL)" Banking : client info / statements / webhooks
ReferenceData "U" --> "D" Banking : currency catalog (Customer-Supplier)
Banking --> Ledger : account validation / provider-account creation
Banking "U (OHS+PL)" --> "D" Integration : public work claims / published facts
Integration --> Ledger : import / reversal / balance observation
Integration --> Banking : fenced completion
Banking "U (OHS+PL)" --> "D" Classification : imported-transaction fact / evidence reads
Ledger "U (OHS+PL)" --> "D" Reporting : accounting facts

note bottom of Integration
  Banking work is also claimed directly by supervised workers.
  Import and observation policies use public context contracts.
  Arrows show capability calls or fact flow as labeled.
end note

legend right
  U = upstream; D = downstream
  OHS+PL = Open Host Service + Published Language
  dashed crimson = Anticorruption Layer
  Ledger owns accounting and reconciliation decisions.
endlegend

@enduml
